      "title": "What is on today’s lunch menu",
      "objective": "Ask what is available today, say what you would like, and request a spoon.",
      "focus": "あります asks about available things. ほしいです says you want an item; 必要です says one is needed. In a restaurant, 〜をお願いします is a polite ordering request. 今日 means today, and 何がありますか asks what is available.",
